          title: "Printable Shopping List & Food Prep Timetable",
          content: "Execution fails not from lack of knowledge but from lack of systems. This chapter provides the complete logistical infrastructure: a store-perimeter-organized shopping list, a 90-minute Sunday prep protocol that yields 80% of weekly meals, and a daily 5-minute assembly workflow. The goal: make the metabolically correct choice the *easiest* choice.\n\n**Shopping List — Organized by Store Perimeter (Shop the Edges, Avoid the Aisles):**\n\n**PRODUCE (30+ distinct species/week — target 40+ for diversity):**\n*Leafy Greens (rotate 3-4 weekly)*: Spinach, arugula, romaine, butter lettuce, Swiss chard, kale, watercress, microgreens\n*Crucifers (daily)*: Broccoli, Brussels sprouts, cauliflower, cabbage (red/green), bok choy, radishes, arugula\n*Alliums (daily)*: Garlic, yellow onion, red onion, shallots, leeks, scallions, chives\n*Colorful Veg*: Bell peppers (3 colors), zucchini, cucumber, celery, carrots, beets, sweet potatoes, tomatoes, eggplant, asparagus, green beans, mushrooms (cremini, shiitake, oyster)\n*Herbs (potent polyphenols)*: Parsley, cilantro, basil, mint, dill, oregano, thyme, rosemary, sage\n*Low-Glycemic Fruit*: Wild blueberries, raspberries, blackberries, strawberries, pomegranate, lemon, lime, avocado, olives, tomato\n*Fermented*: Sauerkraut, kimchi, pickles (refrigerated, unpasteurized), coconut yogurt\n\n**MEAT/SEAFOOD (5-6 proteins, rotate weekly):**\n*Wild-Caught Fish*: Salmon (sockeye/coho), sardines, mackerel, anchovies, herring (SMASH), cod, halibut, scallops, shrimp\n*Grass-Fed/Pastured*: Ground beef (85/15), steak (ribeye, sirloin), liver (1x/week), bone marrow bones, stew meat\n*Poultry*: Pastured chicken (thighs, breasts, whole), turkey, duck\n*Eggs*: Pastured, soy-free (3-4 dozen/week)\n*Bone Broth Ingredients*: Marrow bones, knuckle bones, feet (chicken), oxtail\n\n**PANTRY (15 staples — buy in bulk, glass jars):**\n*Fats*: Extra virgin olive oil (large tin), avocado oil, coconut oil, MCT oil, ghee, grass-fed butter\n*Proteins*: Whey isolate (grass-fed), collagen peptides (Type I/III), gelatin\n*Starches (for cooling)*: White rice (jasmine/basmati), quinoa, buckwheat, oats (steel-cut), potatoes (Yukon gold, sweet)\n*Legumes (soak/sprout)*: Lentils (red, green, black), chickpeas, black beans, white beans\n*Nuts/Seeds*: Almonds, walnuts, macadamia, pecans, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds, chia, flax, hemp\n*Flavor*: Sea salt (Redmond/Celtic), black pepper, turmeric, cinnamon, cumin, paprika, oregano, garlic powder, onion powder\n*Vinegars*: Apple cider (with mother), balsamic, red wine, rice\n*Canned*: Wild sardines, anchovies, tuna, olives, artichoke hearts, tomato paste (tube), coconut milk\n*Supplements*: Berberine, magnesium glycinate, omega-3, D3/K2, NAC, electrolytes\n\n**FROZEN (Convenience + Nutrient Preservation):**\nWild blueberries, mixed berries, spinach, broccoli florets, cauliflower rice, wild fish portions, bone broth cubes\n\n**SUNDAY 90-MINUTE PREP PROTOCOL (Yields 21+ Meals):**\n**Hour 1: Proteins (Simultaneous)**\n1. *Instant Pot Bone Broth*: 3 lbs marrow + 2 lbs knuckle + 2 tbsp ACV + aromatics → 3h high pressure → 12 cups gelatinous broth (freeze 2-cup portions)\n2. *Sheet-Pan Salmon*: 3 lbs wild sockeye + EVOO + lemon + dill + garlic + salt → 400°F 12 min → 6 portions\n3. *Slow-Cooker Shredded Chicken*: 3 lbs bone-in thighs + 2 cups broth + onion + garlic + oregano → 6h low → shred\n\n**Hour 1.5: Vegetables & Starches**\n4. *Cruciferous Medley*: Broccoli, cauliflower, Brussels + EVOO + turmeric + pepper → 425°F 20 min\n5. *Root Vegetable Rainbow*: Sweet potato, carrot, parsnip, beet + EVOO + rosemary → 400°F 35 min → **COOL 12h for RS3**\n6. *Leafy Greens*: Spinach/arugula → quick sauté garlic/EVOO (3 min) OR raw for salads\n7. *Allium Caramelized*: Leeks, onions, garlic → slow 30 min EVOO (preserves inulin)\n8. *Starches*: 3 cups rice + 3 lbs potatoes → cook → spread trays → **COOL 12h at 4°C for RS3**\n\n**Hour 2: Sauces & Assembly**\n9. *Golden Turmeric Tahini*: Tahini + lemon + garlic + turmeric + pepper + ginger + maple + water\n10. *Chimichurri*: Parsley, oregano, cilantro, garlic, red wine vinegar, EVOO, red pepper flakes\n11. *Portion*: 21 glass containers — protein + veg + starch + sauce + fermented\n\n**DAILY 5-MINUTE ASSEMBLY:**\n- Breakfast: Bone broth + eggs + greens + kimchi (2 min)\n- Lunch: Grab container + add EVOO + lemon (1 min)\n- Dinner: Reheat protein + veg + add fresh greens + sauce (3 min)\n\n**COST ANALYSIS**: ~$95-115/week for one person eating 90% organic/grass-fed/wild. Batch cooking reduces waste to <5%. Cost per meal: $4.50-5.50. Compare to $15-25/restaurant meal or $8-12/meal kit. **Health is the ultimate investment — sick care costs 100x more.**\n\n**STORAGE RULES**:\n- Glass containers only (plastic leaches endocrine disruptors when heated)\n- Freeze portions for Days 5-7 (broth, proteins, starches)\n- Sauces last 7-10 days refrigerated\n- Fermented veg last months refrigerated\n- Prep once, eat 21 times — the ultimate efficiency hack.",
